{%- if tools -%}
<start_of_turn>user
You have access to tools and reasoning. Use the following protocol:

1. First, think through the problem inside <reasoning> tags:
<reasoning>
Your reasoning about the task and which tools to use
</reasoning>

2. Then execute the appropriate tool using this JSON format:
<tool_call>
{"name": "<tool_name>", "arguments": {<arguments>}}
</tool_call>

Available tools:
{%- for tool in tools %}
- {{ tool.function.name }}: {{ tool.function.description }}
  Parameters: {{ tool.function.parameters }}
{%- endfor %}
<end_of_turn>
{%- endif -%}
{%- for message in messages -%}
{%- if message['role'] == 'system' -%}
<start_of_turn>user
{{ message['content'] }}<end_of_turn>
{%- elif message['role'] == 'user' -%}
<start_of_turn>user
{{ message['content'] }}<end_of_turn>
{%- elif message['role'] == 'assistant' -%}
<start_of_turn>model
{{ message['content'] }}<end_of_turn>
{%- elif message['role'] == 'tool' -%}
<start_of_turn>user
Tool result for {{ message.get('name', 'unknown') }}: {{ message['content'] }}<end_of_turn>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
<start_of_turn>model
{%- endif -%}
